# Flutter Best Practices

**Flutter skill:** `.cursor/skills/flutter/SKILL.md`  
**Universal gates:** `rules.mdc`

- **MUST** follow Dart null-safety and team `analysis_options.yaml` / linter rules.
- **MUST** handle loading, empty, and error UI for async screens.
- **SHOULD** use one primary state-management pattern per app (Riverpod, Bloc, or team standard).

## Project Structure
- Use feature-first folders under `lib/features/`
- Keep `main.dart` minimal; bootstrap in `lib/app/`
- Colocate tests with features (`test/features/...`)
- Pin dependencies in `pubspec.yaml` with intentional upgrades
- Isolate platform code in `android/`, `ios/`, `web/`

## Widgets
- Prefer StatelessWidget; lift state only when needed
- One primary widget per file for non-trivial UI
- Use composition; avoid deep widget inheritance
- Use `const` constructors for stable subtrees
- Extract widgets when `build` grows or repeats

## State Management
- Local UI state stays near the widget
- App state via Riverpod, Bloc, or agreed library—no ad hoc globals
- Narrow rebuilds (`buildWhen`, selectors, `Consumer` scope)
- Pass IDs through routes; load models in destination

## Navigation
- Use declarative routing (`go_router` or team standard)
- Centralize auth guards and deep links
- Avoid passing large objects in route extras

## Async and Errors
- Use async/await; cancel streams and timers in `dispose`
- Check `mounted` before `setState` after awaits in StatefulWidget
- Map errors to user-safe copy; log with context, no secrets/PII
- Typed failures at repository boundaries

## Performance
- ListView.builder / slivers for long lists
- No heavy sync work on the UI isolate
- Cache network images with explicit dimensions
- Profile with DevTools before blanket RepaintBoundary/memo patterns

## Theming and Accessibility
- Use ThemeData and ColorScheme; avoid scattered magic colors
- Support text scaling and contrast
- Semantics labels on icon-only controls
- Minimum ~48dp touch targets

## Security
- HTTPS in production; secrets only on backend
- Tokens in secure storage, not SharedPreferences
- Parse JSON into typed models before UI use
- Validate platform channel payloads in native code

## Testing
- Unit tests for domain and repositories
- Widget tests for UI states and interactions
- Integration tests for critical user journeys when CI allows
- Mock HTTP and platform boundaries, not business rules in widgets

## Code Organization
- `snake_case.dart` files; `PascalCase` types; `lowerCamelCase` members
- Private API prefixed with `_`
- Document non-obvious business rules briefly
- No business logic inside `build()`
